  "verbalization": "Ent-Gloeosteretriol appears to interact with Atypical kinase COQ8A, mitochondrial through a series of intermediate targets, suggesting a complex network of molecular interactions. The evidence points to Ent-Gloeosteretriol acting as a target for multiple compounds, including Phosphatidylinositol 4-phosphate 3-kinase C2 domain-containing subunit beta and DMS-53, which in turn target COQ8A. These pathways highlight a potential role for Ent-Gloeosteretriol in modulating COQ8A activity, possibly through the activation of downstream signaling cascades. The presence of multiple targets and their shared relationship with COQ8A suggests that Ent-Gloeosteretriol may influence COQ8A function via a broader mechanism, possibly involving the regulation of intracellular signaling or transport processes. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of COQ8A in cellular processes, and the involvement of Ent-Gloeosteretriol may represent a novel or underexplored regulatory mechanism in this context.",
